From: the jellyfin-ffmpeg contributors
Subject: fix hdr10 sidedata not removed in libplacebo outlink
Origin: https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/blob/v8.1.3-2/debian/patches/0085-fix-hdr10-sidedata-not-removed-in-libplacebo-outlink.patch

libplacebo's output loses HDR10's mastering display and light level
metadata when it is no longer HDR10, so an SDR encode isn't tagged with
them.

Rebased onto FFmpeg 9.0.2: the same change, at 9.0.2's line numbers.

From jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-2, where the patch has no header: its authors
are in that repository's history. Under FFmpeg's licence, as the files
it changes.
---
diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c b/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
--- a/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
@@ -1399,6 +1399,16 @@ static int libplacebo_config_output(AVFi
     AVHWFramesContext *hwfc;
     AVVulkanFramesContext *vkfc;
 
+    if (!((s->color_primaries == -1 &&
+           s->color_trc == -1) ||
+          (s->color_primaries == AVCOL_PRI_BT2020 &&
+           s->color_trc == AVCOL_TRC_SMPTE2084))) {
+        av_frame_side_data_remove(&outlink->side_data, &outlink->nb_side_data,
+                                  AV_FRAME_DATA_MASTERING_DISPLAY_METADATA);
+        av_frame_side_data_remove(&outlink->side_data, &outlink->nb_side_data,
+                                  AV_FRAME_DATA_CONTENT_LIGHT_LEVEL);
+    }
+
     /* Frame dimensions */
     RET(ff_scale_eval_dimensions(s, s->w_expr, s->h_expr, inlink, outlink,
                                  &outlink->w, &outlink->h));
